  "name": "catnap — night",
  "note": "It drones as soon as it is loaded. A variation by EG13, not part of the patch: the full catnap rebuild, slower and darker. Part B is the untriggered Plaits chord drone, softer, with the Marbles sequence stepping less than half as often and the Tides swell taking about 8 s instead of 4.8 s over a lower Ripples low-pass; it plays only into part A, where your notes strike a duller, longer Rings bell, and both go into the octave-up Clouds grains, longer, sparser and more reverberant, which freeze and thaw at random, more slowly. Plateau and Warps are left out, as in the full rebuild.",
  "credit": "~zero-g:catnap by plantay (patchstorage.com/zero-gcatnap-vcv-rack-jam)",
  "licence": "CC BY 4.0",
  "order": 7,
